Z||000000||Tigger||11-28-2001||04:02 AM||||FreeWebz.com - free website hosting<BR> <A HREF="http://members.freewebz.com/main.jsp" TARGET=_blank>http://members.freewebz.com/main.jsp</A> <P>Don't waste your time.         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">       <P>I read the hosting features and figured it was well worth looking into.  Nope I've wasted a good hour or two that I should have spent sleeping.         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif">       <P>First they say FTP hosting is an option when you sign up.  Ok cool, I click on a box as I register and boom I can upload using FTP, no big deal, right...  WRONG!  You have to PAY for the FTP option but you don't find out until you're done signing up.  Second, they advertise no ad banners or pop-ups with the free service.  After signing up I find out I have to put some tracking code at the bottom of all of my pages.  Oh, it turns out to be an ad banner at the bottom of the page and I've gota pay if I don't want the tracking code and banner.  What the?  What happened to "free" no banner service?  Lastly, the file manager you use to upload files takes about 4 minutes to upload a simple 3kb image.  They have no option for uploading multiple files at one time...  4 minutes a file, it would take me ages to get my page online.<P>I wouldn't mind paying the few bucks to ditch the banners and get FTP, but the service sucks big time and even trying to bring up links on their site take forever to load.  That doesn't impress me one bit that their own site loads at a snail's pace.  No way I'm going to pay for that.  I read the terms and FAQ's carefully and it seemed too good to be true, well it was.<P>I'm sorry for the rant but I'm desperately looking for a better free - no banners (well ok, small one at the bottom is fine) - (and definitely) no pop up windows - website service.  Fortunecity was a pretty cool service but they have about 3 different pop-ups now that pop up every time you click a link and the ad banners are smack dab at the top of every dang page constantly loading a different ad bogging everything down.  Now I'm looking into other free website services<P>Anyone have any suggestions or know of any good services?<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif">             <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/racingstripes/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||11-28-2001||06:58 AM||||I put a page up at zerocatch <A HREF="http://www.0catch.com" TARGET=_blank>www.0catch.com</A> <BR>It has a banner on top.  I think the freebies are pretty much all the same in the end. BTW I haven't got my links up yet, but do you mind if I add yours again?<P>Gary <A HREF="http://www.grinnin.0catch.com" TARGET=_blank>www.grinnin.0catch.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
